  "worked_solution": "First, we write the given expression as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta -\\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta } & ={tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta -{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor out ${tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta $ and use the identity \n${csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1={cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta .$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta -{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta  & ={tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\,({csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1) \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\,{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
